body:
# Description
This project was aimed to allow continuous development of new collectors as features thanks to it's modular design. Every module must be able to collect data for snapshot purposes and allow _ExposureScout_ to compare two snapshots based on data gathered by those specific modules.

---

We can expect the following list of collector modules to be developed:

## Collectors to develop

- [ ] **_Certificates_**: Collect and list certificates available on the computer;
- [ ] **_Daemons_** and **_Process_**: List daemons and process running on while creating a snapshot (may be separate collectors if needed);
- [ ] **_Cron jobs_**: Collect and list planned jobs;
- [ ] **_Networking_**: Collect and list firewall rules, network interface settings, open ports, host resolution file,...;
- [ ] **_Drivers_**: Collect and list available and currently in use drivers;

## Available
- [x] **_File System_**: Collect and list permissions, sticky bit, size, name ([FileSystem module documentation](https://github.com/Tirette-hub/ExposureScout/blob/main/docs/FSCOLLECTOR.md));
- [x] **_Users_**: Collect and list users, groups, sudoers ([Users module documentation](https://github.com/Tirette-hub/ExposureScout/blob/main/docs/USERSCOLLECTOR.md));

---

If you wish to extend the currently available list of available modules, please consider creating a new project issue with the _enhancement_ label exposing the module you'd implement for tracking purposes.
